t only in repo settings and not in code.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** infra/terraform/github.tf:19 — \"allows_force_pushes\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Force-push and deletion are blocked on main.\n\n`infra/terraform/github.tf` lines 7–31 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   7    owner = \"northbay-clinics\"\n   8  }\n   9  \n  10  data \"github_team\" \"leads\" {\n  11    slug = \"agent-platform-leads\"\n  12  }\n  13  \n  14  resource \"github_branch_protection\" \"main\" {\n  15    repository_id = \"clinic-agent\"\n  16    pattern       = \"main\"\n  17  \n  18    enforce_admins                  = true\n  19>   allows_force_pushes             = false\n  20    allows_deletions                = false\n  21    required_linear_history         = true\n  22    require_signed_commits          = true\n  23    require_conversation_resolution = true\n  24  \n  25    required_pull_request_reviews {\n  26      required_approving_review_count = 2\n  27      require_code_owner_reviews      = true\n  28      dismiss_stale_reviews           = true\n  29      require_last_push_approval      = true\n  30    }\n  31  \n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to B12.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B12\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B12.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n","numLines":169,"startLine":1,"totalLines":169}}}
